==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|revisite}}, from {{der|en|frm|revisiter}} and {{der|en|la|revīsitāre}}, equivalent to {{prefix|en|re|visit}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ɹiːˈvɪzɪt/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-revisit.wav|Audio (Southern England)}}
*: {{rhymes|en|ɪzɪt|s=3}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# To [[visit#Verb|visit]] again.
#* {{quote-book|en|author=[Richard Blackmore]|authorlink=Richard Blackmore|title=A Hymn to the Light of the World. With a Short Description of the Cartons of [[w:Raphael|Raphael Urbin]], in the Gallery at Hampton-Court|location=London|publisher=Printed for {{w|Jacob Tonson}}{{nb...|within Grays-Inn Gate next Grays-Inn Lane.}}|year=1703|page=8|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=lhphAAAAcAAJ&pg=PA8|oclc=40584794|passage=Thou, Kind Redeemer, toucht to ſee / So ſad a Sight, ſuch moving Miſery, / Didſt ſoon determine to diſpel / Theſe Shades of Death, and Gloom of Hell: / And ſo to '''reviſit''' with Thy Heav'nly Light / Loſt Man, bewilder'd in Infernal Night.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1960|month=February|title=Motive Power Miscellany: Scottish Region|journal=Trains Illustrated|page=122|text=On November 21 the restored Highland "Jones Goods" [[4-6-0]], No. 103, '''revisited''' its old haunts when it worked a Stephenson Locomotive Society special from Glasgow (Buchanan Street) to [[Blair Atholl]] and back; [...].}}
# To [[reconsider]] or [[re-experience]] something.

